# `viola-config` BACKLOG

Designed-but-deferred entries for `viola-config`. Items here are decisions made; they ship in the slice that first needs them.

## populate_from_borrowed owned-record fill-in

The `populate_from_borrowed(&self, _borrowed)` method on `ViolaConfigOwned` shipped as a no-op body in Slice 2b. The owned-record fields PluginEntryOwned, GateOwned, RuleOwned, PartialRuleOwned were zero-sized placeholders in Slice 2a; each producer slice flips its owned-record to fields-bearing and fills the projection.

Slice 3 shipped the plugins arm: PluginEntryOwned flipped to a two-field shape (name and path, both Str), the plugins array got the UnsafeCell + Cell interior-mutability wrap, and the populate body now interns each borrowed name and path through the bundled arena and writes the Str pair into each slot. The gates / rules / partial_rules arms remain deferred: validator slices for each will flip their owned-record types to fields-bearing and fill their arms in the same shape (intern through the arena, write into the wrapped owned-array, advance the matching `_len` counter). Each fill needs an UnsafeCell + Cell wrap on the corresponding owned-array per the Slice 3c pattern.
